_exit loads the syscall number into rax and then the status from its input
operand, without telling the compiler it uses rax and rdi. gcc happens to
keep the status elsewhere, but tcc puts it in rax, so every program exited
with status 0x3c. Declare the clobbers, as _write does.

--- a/lib/linux/x86_64-mes-gcc/_exit.c	2026-11-10 15:33:39.490907574 +0100
+++ b/lib/linux/x86_64-mes-gcc/_exit.c	2026-11-10 15:33:39.500111297 +0100
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@
        "syscall \n\t"
        : // no outputs "=" (r)
        : "rm" (code)
+       : "rax", "rdi"
        );
   // not reached
   _exit (0);
